# The Docker build context is the repository root (see deploy/docker-compose.yml
# and deploy/docker/Dockerfile*). Keep it small and free of secrets: everything
# the images need is compiled from source inside the build stages.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build / output artefacts (rebuilt inside the image). Patterns are matched at
# the context root AND nested — `target/` alone would only exclude the repo-root
# Cargo target, leaving `web/frontend/target/` to leak a stale WASM bundle into
# the frontend image (the `dx build` output is rebuilt from source in-stage).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
target/
**/target/
dist/
**/dist/
.dioxus/
**/.dioxus/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test-tooling output and inputs. None of this is built by any image, and all
# of it is expensive to *transfer*: `fuzz/` carries ~11.5k corpus and seed
# files that the context has to walk and hash on each of the ten builds, and
# any touch of one invalidates the `COPY . .` layer for every service image.
#
# `fuzz/` is safe to drop wholesale: it is excluded from the workspace
# (Cargo.toml → `exclude`), pins its own nightly toolchain and carries its own
# lockfile, so nothing `cargo chef prepare` or `cargo build` does in these
# images reads it. `mutants.out*` are cargo-mutants run artefacts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
fuzz/
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VCS / CI / editor / tooling metadata (not needed to build)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.serena/
.junie/
*.iml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docs & repo meta (never copied into an image)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/
**/*.md

# Release and dependency automation. No stage reads these, and leaving them in
# the context made every release commit invalidate `builder`'s `COPY . .` for a
# file nothing compiles. `xtask release-plan` classifies them the same way.
release-please-config.json
.release-please-manifest.json
renovate.json

# `LICENSE` is deliberately NOT excluded, unlike everything above it. PolyForm
# Noncommercial's Notices clause requires the terms to reach anyone who gets a
# copy of any part of the software, and a published image is a copy — so every
# runtime stage in deploy/docker/Dockerfile COPYs it to /LICENSE, which it can
# only do if the file is in the build context. The image contracts under
# deploy/docker/cst/ assert it is there.
#
# `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES` travels with it, for the dependencies' terms rather than
# ours, and is why that file has no extension: `**/*.md` above is a whole-suffix
# exclusion, so a `.md` copy would leave the context and every runtime stage's
# COPY would fail — at the end of a ten-minute build. Regenerate it with
# `cargo run -p xtask -- notices`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local env & secrets (never bake these into an image)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs & OS junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ignore files themselves
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.dockerignore
